Performance artist Derek DelGaudio and director Frank Oz are reteaming for &#8220;Unknown Caller,&#8221; a new stage production that debuts next spring at New York City's Public Theater. The two had collaborated on DelGaudio's unconventional one-man show &#8220;In & Of Itself,&#8221; also directed by Oz, which explored themes of identity and illusion.

Veiled in secrecy, &#8220;Unknown Caller&#8221; is described as a &#8220;new encounter with mystery that asks what we can believe in a counterfeit world&#8221; and promises to &#8220;push the boundaries of storytelling and live performance.&#8221; It will world premiere at the Public's LuEster Hall on March 30. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Disney and the NFL Launch Limited-Edition Mickey & Friends Merch Ahead of Super Bowl LXI Disney Taps Adobe as 'Official AI Innovation Partner' Under Multiyear Pact

"We are becoming more skeptical of what we see and hear," DelGaudio said. "Understandably so, every day we are bombarded by new forgeries and falsehoods. But I have been thinking about what that skepticism costs us. What happens when our first response to something extraordinary is suspicion rather than wonder? That's part of what led me to create &#8216;Unknown Caller.'&#8221;

Oz says working with DelGaudia is like &#8220;jumping off a cliff together into the creative air of uncertainty.&#8221;

